//! The census (ADR-007, D2): a verdict and a one-line reason for every
//! syscall name of the two extracts (385 names; every aarch64 name is also
//! an x86_64 name). `Row` entries are decided by a policy row; `NeedsCap`
//! entries fail because the sandbox holds no capability (D9), with the
//! capability, the kernel function that checks it and the gated forms
//! `capability_gated_calls_fail` calls; `Own` entries act only on the
//! caller's own processes, memory, descriptors, files or namespaces (or
//! read values the sandbox's `/proc` shows anyway); `NotImplemented`
//! entries are `sys_ni_syscall` in every release from 5.19 to 7.2.

use boneli_sys::seccomp::Row;

use super::{Entry, Form, Probe, Verdict};

/// The census, in x86_64 number order, one line per entry.
#[rustfmt::skip]
